To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, add $5$ to both sides of the equation:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{7} \goldE{+5}&=\greenD{x} \goldE{-5} \goldE{+5}\\\\
\greenD{12}= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$

To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\goldE{\text{subtract } 5} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{15}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{15} \goldE{-5} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{10}
\end{align}$
